[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I produced the versioned training dataset **`workspace.mlpab7c22cd.churntraining605fb7`** (Delta version 1) on Databricks, entirely via the platform's SQL warehouse — no local compute.
[agent] **Approach:**
[agent] 1. Created a managed UC volume `workspace.mlpab7c22cd.ingest` and uploaded all six CSVs via `databricks fs cp`.
[agent] 2. Ran all transformation/join work through the SQL Statement Execution API (`/api/2.0/sql/statements`) on the running warehouse `mlpab-grader`.
[agent] 3. Created the table empty (Delta v0) then inserted the join result (Delta **v1**), so version 1 holds the full data.
[agent] **Point-in-time join:** For each of the 100 `labels.csv` rows, I took the most-recent value `WHERE event_time <= label_time` per source table using `ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY account_id, label_time ORDER BY event_time DESC)`, then `LEFT JOIN`ed each feature back to labels on `account_id`. `transactions.csv` and `transactions_late.csv` were `UNION ALL`-merged into one transactions source before the as-of pick.
[agent] **Columns (exactly as required):** account_id, label_time, amount, balance, credit_score, tier, sessions_7d, health_score, churned.
[agent] **Verification:**
[agent] - 100 output rows = 100 label rows (one per label).
[agent] - Zero NULLs across all feature columns.
[agent] - Spot-check on A0000: chose amount 6.55 / balance 3256.67 (the most-recent tx at-or-before label_time), correctly merged the late-export row into the candidate set, correctly excluded a `health_score` reading whose event_time was after label_time, and picked the latest profile (gold/392).
[agent] - `DESCRIBE HISTORY` confirms version 1 = WRITE with the full dataset.
